# Cursor Rules — taste-skill native integration

# When generating UI/UX code in this repository, the following anti-slop
# rules apply. This file is auto-loaded by Cursor for every prompt and
# mirrors `.claude/rules/taste-router.md` + `ui-ux-excellence.md`.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 13 taste-skill variants — pick by prompt signal
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# taste-skill (v2, DEFAULT) — any new frontend brief
# soft-skill — premium / Apple-y / luxury / Awwwards
# minimalist-skill — clean / editorial / Notion-style
# brutalist-skill — Swiss / data-dense / HUD / tactical
# redesign-skill — when user says "redesign" / "audit this UI"
# output-skill — ALWAYS co-load (no placeholders)
# gpt-tasteskill — when target is GPT-4/5/Codex
# taste-skill-v1 — only if user explicitly requests v1
# image-to-code-skill — image-to-code / match a reference
# stitch-skill — Google Stitch DESIGN.md generation
# imagegen-frontend-web — web section image comps
# imagegen-frontend-mobile — iOS / Android screen concepts
# brandkit — brand identity board / logo system

# Source files: .claude/skills/<variant>/SKILL.md

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 3-dial system — declare before any code
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DESIGN_VARIANCE:  1 (symmetric) → 10 (artsy chaos)
# MOTION_INTENSITY: 1 (static) → 10 (cinematic / physics)
# VISUAL_DENSITY:   1 (airy) → 10 (cockpit data-packed)
# Default: 8 / 6 / 4
#
# Brief overrides:
#   minimalist/editorial → V 5-6, M 3-4, D 2-3
#   premium consumer    → V 7-8, M 5-7, D 3-4
#   landing/marketing   → V 7-9, M 6-8, D 3-5
#   data dashboard      → V 4-5, M 2-4, D 7-9
#   trust-first/public  → V 3-4, M 2-3, D 4-5

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Brief inference (MANDATORY — one line before any code)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Reading this as: <page kind> for <audience>, with a <vibe> language, leaning toward <design system>.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 5 anti-slop pillars (matches .github/copilot-instructions.md)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 1. No generic UI — strong typographic hierarchy, alignment care
# 2. Premium whitespace — clamp() over rigid padding
# 3. Cinematic motion — spring physics, never linear easing
# 4. Complete implementation — no `// TODO: add code here`
# 5. Contextual awareness — read .claude/skills/<variant>/SKILL.md

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Banned patterns (the LLM tells)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# - Inter, Roboto, Arial, Open Sans, system-ui (unless a11y constraint)
# - Lucide / Heroicons solid / FontAwesome → use Phosphor Light or Remix Line
# - Purple / indigo gradient backgrounds
# - 3-equal-icon-cards feature grid
# - linear-gradient() on buttons
# - Pure #000000 body text → use #111 or charcoal
# - Centered hero over dark mesh with glassmorphism
# - "Welcome to [App Name]" headings
# - Emoji as icons
# - "// ..." / "rest follows the same pattern" in code

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 18-item pre-flight checklist (declare before "done")
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# [ ] Brief read declared on its own line
# [ ] Dials stated (VARIANCE / MOTION / DENSITY)
# [ ] taste-skill variant identified
# [ ] No banned fonts
# [ ] No banned icons
# [ ] No purple/indigo gradient backgrounds
# [ ] No 3-equal-icon-cards feature grid
# [ ] No linear-gradient on buttons
# [ ] Body text not pure #000000
# [ ] Headlines letter-spacing -0.02em to -0.04em
# [ ] Layout symmetric OR explicitly asymmetric with intent
# [ ] No emoji as icons
# [ ] No "Welcome to [App Name]" headings
# [ ] All CTAs are full sentences / specific verbs
# [ ] output-skill enforced: no placeholders
# [ ] All interactive elements Tab + Enter/Space accessible
# [ ] Dark mode token set declared
# [ ] Mobile collapse strategy explicit
# Gate: 3+ fail → regenerate. 1-2 fail → fix inline.

# For deep style configs, read .claude/skills/<variant>/SKILL.md.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Impeccable coexistence (pbakaus upstream)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The repo also ships [impeccable](https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable) at
# .cursor/skills/impeccable/ (and 11 other harness dirs) — a vocabulary-first
# design skill with 23 commands and 27 anti-pattern rules.
#
# When to load which:
#   /impeccable <cmd> or named commands (audit, polish, critique, distill,
#     harden, animate, bolder, quieter, typeset, layout, colorize, adapt,
#     onboard, overdrive, delight, optimize, clarify, extract, document,
#     init, shape, craft, live) → load impeccable from .cursor/skills/
#   shape picker (Soft / Minimalist / Brutalist) or 3-dial spec
#     (VARIANCE / MOTION / DENSITY) → load taste-skill (already above)
#
# Both ban the same LLM tells. The 18-item pre-flight above is for
# taste-skill; impeccable ships its own 27-rule anti-pattern detector
# (run via `npx impeccable detect <path>` — uses the impeccable npm CLI,
# already installed alongside the skill).
#
# Pair order: impeccable FIRST (vocabulary + brand-vs-product register),
# taste-skill SECOND (dials + variant for the build). Cross-check both
# pre-flight checklists before declaring done.
